.SH NAME
env \- set environment for command execution
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B env
.RB [ \- ]
[ \fIname\fB=\fIvalue\fR ] ...
[ command args ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Env\^
obtains the current
.IR environment ,
modifies it according to its arguments,
then executes the command with the modified environment.
Arguments of the form
.IB name = \fIvalue\fR
are merged into the inherited environment
before the command is executed.
.PP
If no command is specified, the resulting environment
is printed, one
.IB name = value
pair per line.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-
Cause the inherited environment to be ignored completely,
so that the command is executed with exactly the environment
specified by the arguments.
.SH SEE ALSO
sh(1), csh(1), exec(2), environ(5).
